  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The specimen bench",
    "overview": "The specimen bench is a light native workbench: the actual output occupies the center, experiment history sits on the left, and the selected result is explained on the right. Code, timings and compiler diagnostics share a lower dock. This direction was implemented under the user's delegated brief; it is not recorded as an approved visual comp.\n\nWhite surfaces, compact sans-serif labels and straight panel seams keep attention on the data. Color marks actions, selection and measured output. Native meshes and netlists are the imagery; promotional illustration and ornamental cards have no role here.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "A/B output remains central and registered.",
      "History, inspector and code occupy stable work areas.",
      "White surfaces and blue interaction states; no green or lime.",
      "Rendering responds to data, resize and interaction rather than a continuous animation loop."
